**Worksheet**

F1: state{}, makeRng(), endTurn() calls resolveProduction→resolveNeeds→rollEvent→finishTurnTail in fixed order. Score 2.

F2: genGrid() builds 64-tile grid from rng; canBuild() checks b.terrain.includes(tile.terrain); adjacencyMultiplier() changes production output. Score 2.

F3: forge consumes ore+power→metal, greenhouse consumes soil+water→food; RES_CAPS enforced with overflow logged and lost. Score 2.

F4: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job/tile; skillMul and moraleFactor(worker.morale) read in resolveProduction. Score 2.

F5: resolveNeeds() consumes food/water, shortage sets moraleDelta -8; moraleFactor() scales output; fatigue<40 grants +2 morale (recoverable). Score 2.

F6: 11 RESEARCH nodes, canResearch() enforces prereqs+cost, metallurgy/hydroponics multiply yields in resolveProduction, stormWallEng/stormPrediction feed mitigationFactor(). Score 2.

F7: 12 EVENTS, weighted pick via totalWeight loop; 6 events (wanderers, sickness, dispute, toxiccloud, drifter, malfunction) have branching choices; events.cooldowns tracked/ticked. Score 2.

F8: priceFor() reads supplyDemand (drifted) and stock/cap pressure; tradeBuy/tradeSell mutate scrip+res+caravan item.qty. Score 2.

F9: resolveStorm() damages tile.hp; production only reduced when disabledTurns>0 (binary), partially-damaged (hp<100) tiles still produce at full rate; doRepair() spends 5 parts; mitigationFactor() from stormwall/research. Score 1 (damage doesn't scale output until full disable).

F10: serialize()=JSON.stringify(state) into textarea; deserialize() validates required fields and JSON.parse try/catch with saveMsg error text. Score 2.

F11: checkEndConditions() sets phase 'won'/'lost' from turn/pop/shortage; computeScore() combines pop/research/stock/turn; renderEndScreen() shows summary modal. Score 2.

F12: switchTab() wires tab buttons; renderLog() shows l.turn; tip()/showTip() tooltips on chips/buttons; keydown handler for Space/1-5; @media(max-width:400px) layout rules. Score 2.

F13: runTests() asserts RNG determinism, terrain/prereq enforcement, morale/shortage, save/load hash equality, win/lose; runBenchmark() runs 200 headless turns via greedyPolicyTurn() and prints stateHash(). Score 2.

G1: st.research.metallurgy.done and hydroponics.done read directly in resolveProduction's out*=1.25 branches, applied every relevant turn. Score 4.

G2: resolveNeeds() shortage → c.morale -=8 → moraleFactor(worker.morale) scales output in resolveProduction, chain runs every turn. Score 4.

G3: tile.hp reduced by storm but only disabledTurns>0 (hp<=0 case) stops production; partial-damage tiles produce at full rate; doRepair() restores hp/disabledTurns for 5 parts. Score 2 (binary special-case, not graduated loss).

G4: priceFor() multiplies base by st.trade.supplyDemand[res] (drifts via driftSupplyDemand) and by local stock/cap pressure, used in both tradeBuy/tradeSell. Score 4.

G5: wanderers choice mutates res.food/addColonist vs res.scrip+morale; malfunction choice sets tile.disabledTurns/hp vs spends parts — both durable grid/resource state changes, not just log text. Score 4.

